ore is the all-zeros SHA (first push) or a non-ancestor (force-push) — whether it selects nothing, errors, or falls back to a resolvable base — and align the ref derivation so a rubric edit on a branch's first push is still detected.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.297,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: push trigger 'passing --changed-since ${{ github.event.before }}'","github.event.before is all-zeros (0000000…) on the first push to a new branch and a non-ancestor SHA after a force-push — VERIFIED as a standard GitHub Actions push-event behavior","Reused primitive drift_floor._drifted_paths (drift_floor.py:37-61) returns None on '(missing SHA, unknown HEAD, git error)'; the plan does not state how the new selection mode maps that None (select nothing vs. error vs. fall back)","Plan's enumerated CLI-precondition classes are only Verified for pull_request (base.sha, well-defined) — the push-before ref is Unverified/Contradicted for the first-push and force-push cases"],"finding":"The CI integration relies on the GitHub Actions context github.event.before resolving to a diffable git ref for the push trigger, but on a branch's first push it is the all-zeros SHA (and after a force-push a non-ancestor), so `git diff --name-only <before>..HEAD` errors or produces a meaningless set — an unstated precondition of the changed-file range integration.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f57fdca6b57b925a5","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'CI trigger classification and ref derivation' and 'Range → changed files'","norm_id":"n25c6884853359299","priority":0.603,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A rubric edit lands on the first push of a new branch (before = 0000…): git diff against the zero SHA errors and the job either silently selects nothing (missing the regression it exists to catch) or fails the step","A force-push rewrites branch history: before is no longer an ancestor of HEAD and the diff range is meaningless"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"For push, derive the base from a resolvable ref (e.g. merge-base against the default branch, or fall back to HEAD~1 when github.event.before is 000…/non-ancestor); explicitly specify that an uncomputable range maps to a stated selection outcome and exit code rather than an unhandled git error.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify selection behavior for an uncomputable `--changed-since` range (all-zeros/absent/non-ancestor base, e.g. first push or force-push): state whether it selects nothing, errors, or falls back, and align the CI `push` ref derivation so a rubric edit on a branch's first push is still detected.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Range → changed files reuses the existing `git diff --name-only <ref>..HEAD` plumbing shape … (`plan_review.drift_floor._drifted_paths`)'","Plan: push trigger 'passing `--changed-since ${{ github.e